    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d532">

                <pb facs="0978" n="964" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg964"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.CC/10–644</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Mr.
                            Myron C. Taylor, Personal Representative of
                        President Roosevelt to Pope Pius
                            XII
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 12</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-06">October 6,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Secretary of State encloses an official copy in English of the “Proposals for
                    the Establishment of a General International Organization”<anchor n="14"
                        xml:id="d532-f1"/> which have been agreed upon by the British, Soviet,
                    Chinese and the United States delegations to the Dumbarton Oaks conversations
                    and have been submitted to their respective governments.</p>
                <p>The Personal Representative of the President at the Vatican should deliver the
                    enclosed copy informally to His Holiness the Pope, pointing out that this
                    document represents only the tentative proposals reported to their respective
                    governments by the delegations to the; Dumbarton Oaks conversations.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d532-f1" n="14" xml:id="d532-f1-content">
                <p>For text of the Dumbarton Oaks Proposals, see <ref target="#pg890">p.
                    890</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
